0.22+20250801+lc1 (2026-11-19)
  * ORDER 40: the headers and the example of SenseGlove's C++ API (github.com/Adjuvo/SenseGlove-API, MIT), commit 31900b320aa0 (2025-08-01), each file checked against sources.tsv; a CMake package (find_package(SenseGlove), targets SenseGlove::SGCore and SenseGlove::SGConnect); a CMakeLists.txt for the example.
  * The libraries libsgcore and libsgconnect are SenseGlove's binaries with no published source: not in this package. Stereo APTus fetches them from SenseGlove when the person installs the entry "SenseGlove API libraries (C++)"; until then find_package says so and names the entry.
  * The libraries are built with LLVM's libc++ (measured on v20, v21 and v22: std::__1 in every exported name): the CMake targets add -stdlib=libc++ for Clang and refuse another compiler, and README.Debian says so. With g++ SenseGlove's own example does not link on Debian (undefined reference to SGCore::HapticGlove::ToString[abi:cxx11](SGCore::EHapticLocation), then to every std type of the API).
